{"title":"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Four circles of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are each tangent to two sides of a square and externally tangent to a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, as shown. What is the area of the square?\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/23759fb5d0c074107da579ab5ce358f0aa30b5a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(5mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(8pt)); real h=3*sqrt(2)/2; pair O0=(0,0), O1=(h,h), O2=(-h,h), O3=(-h,-h), O4=(h,-h); pair X=O0+2*dir(30), Y=O2+dir(45); draw((-h-1,-h-1)--(-h-1,h+1)--(h+1,h+1)--(h+1,-h-1)--cycle); draw(Circle(O0,2)); draw(Circle(O1,1)); draw(Circle(O2,1)); draw(Circle(O3,1)); draw(Circle(O4,1)); draw(O0--X); draw(O2--Y); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,midpoint(O0--X),NW); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,midpoint(O2--Y),SE); [/asy]\" width=\"152\" height=\"152\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4b160d78586d1536ea827a2b8f1bc82d0e7f4f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 32 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 22 + 12\\sqrt {2}\\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 16 + 16\\sqrt {3}\\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 48 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 36 + 16\\sqrt {2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"570\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw a square connecting the centers of the four small circles of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This square has a diagonal of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, as it includes the diameter of the big circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and two radii of the small circles of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the side length of this square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9ae6a28635f7bc2f1d620576f68cea4d8a917152.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}} = 3\\sqrt{2}.\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"42\" /> The side length of the larger square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units greater than the one found by connecting the midpoints, so its side length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8d2199d03dc28d51bf35318bfa8e414d50d207.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 + 3\\sqrt{2}.\\]\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> The area of the larger square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7eef8908ce046151531150a7f8cf21c3ce53d69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2+3\\sqrt{2})^2 = 22 + 12\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"193\" height=\"21\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/7400154b2e9fb4e72cd6e18c14b9a4e964737ed0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(B).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We draw the diagonal of the square. This diagonal yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f57d642e33f5b59a4aa2614f138cfe87ea478ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{2}+1+1+2+2=2\\sqrt{2}+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"247\" height=\"18\" />. We know that the side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> in terms of the diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/8/7e8e00339ae98c3c7ad90164e5dc67345929655d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=\\frac{d}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"59\" height=\"42\" />, so our side length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e11d5317e0c3204e8a90a5a5851ad8ccaa858b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}+6}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"67\" height=\"45\" />. However, we are trying to look for the area, so squaring <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e11d5317e0c3204e8a90a5a5851ad8ccaa858b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}+6}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"67\" height=\"45\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f461ab91ddd73e8c976935c21bcc6421efcf3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{44+24\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\boxed{\\text{(B)}22+12\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"230\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Connect the points from centre of big circle to the top 2 circles. This creates a right isosceles triangle of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c40d25bf3b35c55768d241a0121ad6dc12cd2865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+1=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. Thus its hypotenuse is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/5/005458b4333cedea7a3aa771f6620c976597f9af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Adding twice the radius of the top circle gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cba3da7d60f9a93c00b5ca92198214f4cdc904d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+3\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. This is the side length of the square, thus its area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd514432b36f3273c0584f3f0904a43ada6209b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B)}22+12\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"121\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>I'm bad at explaining things I'm sure its understandable with diagram\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A\">2007 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195047\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 221/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4934/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.206      1 -total\n 60.70%    8.016      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.25%    5.051      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6319:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017195047 and revision id 282902. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}